Week 7: Social Media Strategy / The Grammys 🎵
Project: Social Media Campaign & Analytics / The Grammys 🎵

In this project, you’ll define the strategy for a paid social media campaign for one of the biggest events in the entertainment industry: the Grammy Awards. You’ll start by crafting a campaign plan with clear objectives, 
a defined audience, and platform-specific ad types. If you are interested in analytics, you'll have a chance to LevelUp and dive into the numbers to assess what's working based on core metrics like CPA, CPC, and CTR. 
And finally, you'll draft a LinkedIn post about what you've learned. 

 

YOUR TASK

To begin your social media campaign, carefully review the campaign brief (linked in the slides below)—especially the “overview” and “objective” sections—to determine a clear objective for your campaign. Next, 
select a customer persona to focus on; several options are provided in the brief. Read through your chosen persona in detail, as this audience will guide the development of your campaign strategy. Based on this persona, 
create specific targeting criteria to ensure your ads reach the right audience. Then, choose the most effective social media channels and ad types to deliver your message and achieve your objective. For those looking to 
go further, you can LevelUp with extra credit by analyzing your campaign data—calculate cost efficiency metrics and interpret the results to evaluate campaign performance. Also, you can create a LinkedIn post to level 
up and share your work with a broader audience.
